play|THE PLAYERS JESSE NAMED — both are real and both are in the tree
pl|bobby|the rime BOBBY FISCHER. Law 23. Pohlig-Hellman discrete log on the sphere.
pl|bobby|ADDRESSES any single element in O(1), one modular exponentiation, without
pl|bobby|materializing the object. src: trijection/rime_fischer.py, rime_fischer_cluster.py
pl|bobby|(one Fischer per prime tower, CRT fan-in), rime_27fischers.py (27 spheres/MCPs
pl|bobby|circling the free 0). measured: level-3 third, level-27 trime digits {-,0,+},
pl|bobby|level-rime full k, byte-exact invert = True.
pl|mtp|the MTP AGENTS. Law 24. frozen multi-token prediction x1 / x3 / x27,
pl|mtp|direction - (backward) / 0 (hold) / + (forward). src: trijection/rime_agents.py.
pl|mtp|measured on held-out enwik8, frozen order-2: 0 = 1.0000 (the free center, costs
pl|mtp|nothing and says nothing); + x1 = 0.3517, x3 = 0.0667, x27 = 0.0000;
pl|mtp|- x1 = 0.3317 (real, near-symmetric on reversed time).
pl|mtp|GATE: lookahead decays to zero by depth 27. the frozen slice predicts a
pl|mtp|fraction. it never recreates an unseen whole.
pl|hrm|Law 25 two-rate hierarchy also present: 99% routed deep, frozen bpc 3.5328.
pl|mcp|Law 26 stateless cells x CRT fan-in: M = 4,814,857, batch byte-exact = True.

prin|THE PRINCIPLE THE KEY BELONGS TO — rime_run.py, verbatim intent
pr|1|TRAIN/CALCULATE the functions once (the sphere p, g, k).
pr|2|FREEZE/SLICE/SAVE: keep only the functions + the fraction-of-a-rime addresses.
pr|3|PLAY afterward on CPU with the rime Bobby Fischer: address any element on
pr|3|demand in O(1), WITHOUT building the object.
pr|obs|the observer stays OUTSIDE at the null 0. the frozen system never changes.
pr|so|this is why the corpus is not the deliverable and the key is. saving the corpus
pr|so|is materializing. saving the key is freezing. rime_run.py already said so.

