law|NEW LAW — THE SHIPPED PRIOR CAN NEVER PAY FOR ITSELF
lw|010|return rate falls with size: 579/3174 = 18.24%, 2377/31740 = 7.49%,
lw|010|10818/317400 = 3.41%, 37369/3174000 = 1.18%. four points, monotone.
lw|011|fit: saving ~ S^0.603 (log-log slope over three decades = 0.603).
lw|011|break-even needs saving >= S, which holds only below S ~ 44 bytes.
lw|011|therefore no shipped distant prior of any useful size pays for itself IN ONE
lw|011|MONOLITHIC STREAM. amended 2026-07-27 (ERRATA-1): under SECTIONING it DOES
lw|011|pay - saving is a fixed transient per cold model start, recurs per section,
lw|011|charge paid once, break-even 5.31 sections, 36/36 byte-exact.
